    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Exceptional Four-Bedroom Dormer Bungalow with Generous Gardens.\r\n\r\nSet in a desirable and established location on Dispensary Lane, Rathfarnham, this impressive four-bedroom dormer bungalow offers well-proportioned accommodation, excellent versatility and an enviable connection between the living spaces and the private rear garden.\r\n\r\nFrom the moment you enter, the sense of space is immediately apparent. The exceptionally generous lounge forms the heart of the home and features bi-fold doors opening directly onto a substantial decking area. Overlooking the rear garden, this wonderful space is perfectly suited to both relaxed family living and entertaining, while the large glazed opening floods the room with natural light.\r\nThe kitchen and dining room provide a superb everyday living space, with direct access to the rear garden and offers a separate utility off. The layout lends itself particularly well to modern family life, offering an excellent balance of informal dining, entertaining and outdoor living.\r\nThe ground floor also benefits from a well-appointed bedroom with ensuite, making it an ideal guest suite or private accommodation for family members. A guest WC and understairs storage further enhance the practicality of the ground floor.\r\n\r\nUpstairs, there are three further well-proportioned bedrooms, along with a main family bathroom. An additional dedicated office room provides an excellent and increasingly valuable space for working from home, studying or pursuing hobbies.\r\n\r\nThe rear garden is a particular feature of the property, with the decking area providing an attractive extension of the main living accommodation and a wonderful setting for outdoor dining and entertaining.\r\n\r\nCombining generous accommodation, versatile living space and an excellent indoor-outdoor flow, this impressive dormer bungalow offers a wonderful opportunity to acquire a spacious family home in one of Rathfarnham's established residential settings."
      },
